    <bpmn:process id="W_W1117" name="W1117. Customer Trade Account Statement of Account Auto-Generation &amp; Email Delivery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly statement generation schedule (1st business day of the month), or customer request for on-demand statement
Frequency: Monthly (scheduled); on-demand (customer request via portal, phone, or email)
Volume: ~5,200 trade accounts × 1 statement/month = ~5,200 scheduled statements; ~500 on-demand requests/month
Owner: AR Analyst (Finance)
Participants: AR Analyst, Customer (Trade Account Holder), IT (system configuration)
Source: workflow W1117 — Customer Trade Account Statement of Account Auto-Generation &amp; Email Delivery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1117_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1117_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1117_Lane2" name="AR Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1117_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1117_Start4" name="Monthly statement generation schedule (1st business day of the month), or customer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1117_Task5" name="Monthly Scheduled SOA Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly Scheduled SOA Generation: (a) on the 1st business day of each month, system automatically generates SOAs for all active trade accounts with non-zero balances: (i) pulls all AR transactions for the prior month: invoices (W8), payments received (W556), credit notes (W101), debit notes, adjustments; (ii) calculates: opening balance (as of 1st of prior month), total invoices, total payments, total credits, total debits, closing balance (as of last day of prior month), current portion (0–30 days), past due portions (31–60, 61–90, 90+ days); (iii) includes BIR-compliant information: BuildRight TIN, trade customer TIN, registered business names and addresses; (b) system formats SOA as PDF: (i) BuildRight branded header; (ii) trade account name, address, and account number; (iii) itemized transaction table (date, reference, description, debit, credit, running balance); (iv) aging summary; (v) payment instructions (bank details: BDO/BPI/Metrobank account numbers); (vi) AR contact information for inquiries; (vii) &quot;Questions about your statement? Contact [email] or [phone]&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AR Analyst
Duration: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1117_Task6" name="Automated Email Delivery &amp; Portal Publishing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated Email Delivery &amp; Portal Publishing: (a) system emails SOA to the trade account&#x27;s designated billing contact email: (i) email subject: &quot;BuildRight Depot — Statement of Account for [Account Name] — [Month Year]&quot;; (ii) body: brief summary (total due, due date, link to self-service portal); (iii) PDF attached; (iv) BCC to AR team email for tracking; (b) system simultaneously publishes SOA to the trade account&#x27;s self-service portal (W936): (i) customer logs into portal to view, download, or print SOA; (ii) portal retains 24-month SOA history; (iii) portal shows real-time AR balance (not just month-end); (c) system logs delivery status: sent, delivered, bounced, opened (if email tracking enabled); (d) bounced emails flagged for AR Analyst review: contact may have changed — update customer master (W508)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AR Analyst
Duration: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1117_Task7" name="On-Demand SOA Request Handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: On-Demand SOA Request Handling: (a) trade customer requests statement via: (i) self-service portal (W936) — instant download of most recent SOA or custom date range statement; (ii) email to AR team — auto-generated response with portal link, or manual email within 4 hours; (iii) phone call to customer service (W259) — agent generates and emails SOA during the call; (b) for on-demand requests specifying a custom date range (e.g., &quot;last 6 months consolidated&quot;), system generates an ad-hoc SOA with the same format but for the specified period; (c) all on-demand requests logged for tracking (frequency, reason, channel)
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service
Accountable (A): AR Analyst
Duration: 1–5 min (self-service); 10–15 min (manual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1117_Task8" name="SOA Dispute Handling &amp; Reconciliation Support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SOA Dispute Handling &amp; Reconciliation Support: (a) if trade customer disputes their SOA: (i) customer submits dispute via portal (W869 — vendor dispute resolution adapted for customer disputes) or email; (ii) dispute categorized: missing payment (customer paid but not credited), unrecognized invoice, incorrect amount, duplicate charge, credit note not reflected; (iii) AR Analyst investigates: (a) checks bank statement for missing payment — if received but unapplied, applies to customer account; (b) pulls invoice copy from document management (W255) for unrecognized charge; (c) verifies credit note posting for missing credits; (iv) resolution communicated within 5 business days; (v) if SOA was incorrect, corrected SOA generated and re-sent; (vi) dispute resolution tracked for aging (W889) and root cause analysis (W507)
Responsible (R): AR Analyst
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1117_Task9" name="Monthly SOA Delivery Effectiveness Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly SOA Delivery Effectiveness Reporting: (a) system generates monthly SOA delivery report: (i) total SOAs generated; (ii) delivery success rate (target: ≥ 99%); (iii) bounce rate and reasons; (iv) portal self-service access rate (% of customers who viewed SOA on portal vs. email only); (v) on-demand request volume and average response time; (vi) dispute rate (% of SOAs disputed) and resolution time; (vii) correlation between SOA delivery and payment speed (accounts that view SOA within 3 days pay 5 days faster on average); (b) report reviewed by AR Manager for process improvement
Responsible (R): System / AR Analyst
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: 30 min/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1117_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1117_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1117_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1117_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-185 (ensure B2B billing &amp; receivable milestone integrity.) | - operational: AR Analyst (Finance) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AR Analyst (Finance)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1117_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1117_Annotation11" targetRef="W1117_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow13" sourceRef="W1117_Start4" targetRef="W1117_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow14" sourceRef="W1117_Task5" targetRef="W1117_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow15" sourceRef="W1117_Task6" targetRef="W1117_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow16" sourceRef="W1117_Task7" targetRef="W1117_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow17" sourceRef="W1117_Task8" targetRef="W1117_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1117_Flow18" sourceRef="W1117_Task9" targetRef="W1117_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1117_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1117_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1117">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_End10_di" bpmnElement="W1117_End10"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1117_Annotation11_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Annotation11"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1117_Assoc12_di" bpmnElement="W1117_Assoc12"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
