    <bpmn:process id="W_W1269" name="W1269. Customer Trade Account Application, Credit Assessment &amp; Onboarding" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (contractor, builder, interior designer, architect, or business) applies for a BuildRight trade account with credit terms
Frequency: ~40–60 new trade account applications/month across 200 stores; ~500–700/year
Volume: Each application processed individually; total active trade accounts: ~5,200
Owner: Trade Account Manager (HQ)
Participants: Sales Associate (store-level intake), Trade Account Manager, Credit Analyst, Finance Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W1269 — Customer Trade Account Application, Credit Assessment &amp; Onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1269_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1269_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1269_Lane2" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1269_Lane3" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1269_Lane4" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1269_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1269_Start6" name="Customer (contractor, builder, interior designer, architect, or business) applies for a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task7" name="In-store application intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: In-store application intake: customer approaches Sales Associate or Customer Service Rep requesting trade account; Sales Associate provides trade account application form (paper or digital tablet); customer provides: (a) business name and DTI/SEC registration number, (b) owner/principal name and government-issued ID (passport, driver&#x27;s license, national ID), (c) business address and contact details, (d) trade references (other suppliers with credit terms), (e) estimated monthly purchase volume, (f) requested credit limit, (g) authorized purchasers (names and IDs of employees allowed to purchase on account), (h) BIR-registered TIN (Tax Identification Number)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task8" name="Application submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Application submission: Sales Associate scans/uploads application and supporting documents (DTI/SEC registration, government IDs, TIN certificate, trade references) to Trade Account Management system; application assigned unique reference number; Sales Associate provides customer with application reference and estimated processing timeline (3–5 business days for trade accounts, 5–10 for corporate accounts)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task9" name="Application verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Application verification: Trade Account Manager reviews submitted application: (a) verifies DTI/SEC registration number against online government database, (b) verifies TIN format and validity, (c) contacts trade references (minimum 2 required) to confirm credit history and payment behavior, (d) checks BuildRight internal records — does applicant have existing personal purchases, returns history, or loyalty account?, (e) checks negative list — has applicant or principals been involved in fraud, bounced checks (W1381), or account write-offs with BuildRight previously?
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task10" name="Credit assessment and scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Credit assessment and scoring: Credit Analyst evaluates application using scoring model: (a) Business stability score (0–30 points): years in operation, business registration type (sole prop vs. corporation), number of employees, (b) Trade reference score (0–25 points): quality of trade references, payment behavior reported by references, (c) Financial capacity score (0–25 points): estimated annual revenue, bank statements (if provided for higher limits), existing credit obligations, (d) Relationship score (0–20 points): existing BuildRight loyalty membership, length of prior cash purchases, referral source; total score maps to risk tier: (i) Low Risk (70–100): standard approval, credit limit per scoring matrix, (ii) Medium Risk (50–69): conditional approval, lower credit limit, shorter terms (Net 15 instead of Net 30), (iii) High Risk (below 50): decline or offer pre-paid/cash-only account with trade pricing
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task11" name="Credit limit determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Credit limit determination: Credit Analyst determines credit limit based on: (a) requested amount vs. scoring result, (b) industry benchmarks: contractors PHP 50K–500K, interior designers PHP 100K–1M, developers PHP 500K–5M, (c) business tenure and trade reference quality, (d) initial conservative limit (typically 50% of requested) with automatic review after 6 months of good payment history; proposed credit limit and terms submitted to Finance Manager for approval
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task12" name="Approval decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Approval decision: Finance Manager reviews credit assessment and proposed terms; decision: (a) Approved — as proposed, (b) Approved with modified terms — different limit, shorter terms, or additional conditions (e.g., post-dated checks required), (c) Declined — with reason; customer notified of decision within 5 business days of application; if declined, customer offered trade pricing on a cash/pre-paid basis (trade account without credit)
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task13" name="Account setup in ERP">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Account setup in ERP: Trade Account Manager creates customer account: (a) customer master record with business details, authorized purchasers, and credit limit, (b) trade pricing tier assignment (5–15% discount per §9.3), (c) payment terms (Net 30 standard, Net 15 for conditional), (d) credit limit enforced in POS — any purchase exceeding available credit triggers block and Store Manager override request, (e) authorized purchaser IDs linked to account for POS verification, (f) statement delivery preference (email, physical mail)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task14" name="Customer welcome and activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Customer welcome and activation: Trade Account Manager sends welcome package to customer: (a) trade account card (with account number and authorized purchaser names), (b) credit limit and terms confirmation, (c) trade pricing overview, (d) POS usage instructions — authorized purchaser presents trade account card + valid ID at checkout, (e) online account portal registration (view statements, transaction history), (f) account manager contact information, (g) credit policy summary: payment deadlines, late payment consequences, credit limit review schedule
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1269_Task15" name="First purchase monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: First purchase monitoring: Trade Account Manager monitors first 3 months of trade account activity: (a) purchase frequency and volume vs. estimated, (b) payment timeliness (first 3 invoices), (c) authorized purchaser compliance (no unauthorized charges), (d) after 3 months: if payment behavior is good, account confirmed at current terms; if late payments, terms tightened or limit reduced per W1245
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15 min/month (first 3 months)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1269_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1269_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1269_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1269_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: Trade Account Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Account Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1269_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1269_Annotation17" targetRef="W1269_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
