    <bpmn:process id="W_W1394" name="W1394. Customer Trade Account Annual Credit Review, Tier Reclassification &amp; Terms Adjustment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — annual credit review cycle for all active trade accounts; ad-hoc triggered by significant payment deterioration or material change in customer&#x27;s financial condition
Frequency: Annual comprehensive review for all ~5,200 trade accounts; ad-hoc reviews for ~200–300 accounts/year triggered by alerts
Volume: ~5,200 accounts reviewed annually; ~800–1,200 tier reclassifications/year
Owner: Credit Manager
Participants: Credit Analyst, Credit Manager, Head of Trade / Account Management, Finance Manager, CFO
Source: workflow W1394 — Customer Trade Account Annual Credit Review, Tier Reclassification &amp; Terms Adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1394_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1394_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1394_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1394_Lane3" name="Credit Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1394_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1394_Start5" name="Scheduled — annual credit review cycle for all active trade accounts; ad-hoc triggered by…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1394_Task6" name="Annual review batch generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual review batch generation (Q1 each year): system generates annual credit review list for all active trade accounts: (a) current tier (Tier 1: Net 30, Tier 2: Net 45, Tier 3: Net 60, Tier 4: Net 90), (b) current credit limit, (c) 12-month payment performance: average days to pay, number of late payments, bounced checks (W1381), credit holds triggered, (d) 12-month purchase volume and trend (growing/declining/stable), (e) outstanding AR balance, (f) credit insurance status (W1011)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1394_Task7" name="Automated scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated scoring: credit scoring engine re-computes risk score for each account: (a) payment score (weight 40%): average days to pay vs. terms, on-time payment %, number of bounced checks; (b) volume score (weight 20%): annual purchase volume and growth trend; (c) financial score (weight 20%): updated financial statement analysis (if customer provided), industry risk, years in business; (d) external score (weight 20%): credit bureau data (if available), SEC/DTI filing status, trade references; (e) composite risk score: 1 (lowest risk) to 5 (highest risk)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1394_Task8" name="Tier reclassification recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Tier reclassification recommendation: system recommends tier change based on updated risk score: (a) Risk Score 1 → Tier 4 (Net 90, highest credit limit); (b) Risk Score 2 → Tier 3 (Net 60); (c) Risk Score 3 → Tier 2 (Net 45); (d) Risk Score 4 → Tier 1 (Net 30, reduced limit); (e) Risk Score 5 → hold/suspend per W1395; (f) system flags accounts where recommended tier differs from current tier for Credit Analyst review
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1394_Task9" name="Credit Analyst review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Credit Analyst review (for flagged accounts — estimated ~1,500–2,000 accounts): Credit Analyst reviews each flagged account: (a) agree with system recommendation?; (b) if disagree: document reason (e.g., &quot;customer had one bounced check due to bank error — should not result in downgrade&quot;); (c) for downgrade recommendations: Sales Rep consulted — Sales Rep may provide context (e.g., &quot;customer just completed large project, purchasing will resume next quarter&quot;) that argues against downgrade; (d) for upgrade recommendations: Credit Analyst verifies customer financial capacity supports higher exposure
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 15–20 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1394_Task10" name="Credit limit adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Credit limit adjustment: for each tier reclassification, Credit Analyst recomputes credit limit: (a) new limit = recommended tier&#x27;s standard limit formula (e.g., Tier 3: average monthly purchases × 2 months); (b) adjusted for customer-specific factors (industry risk, concentration, collateral); (c) ensure new limit does not exceed credit insurance coverage (W1011)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 5 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1394_Task11" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Approval: tier changes and limit adjustments approved per authority matrix: (a) Tier upgrade + limit increase ≤ PHP 500K: Credit Manager approves; (b) Tier upgrade + limit increase &gt; PHP 500K: CFO approves; (c) Tier downgrade: Credit Manager approves (no escalation needed — Credit Manager has authority to tighten terms); (d) account suspension: per W1395
Responsible (R): Credit Manager / CFO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 5–10 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1394_Task12" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer notification: Credit Analyst prepares customer notification for all tier changes: (a) upgrade notification — congratulatory, outlines new terms and limit, effective date; (b) downgrade notification — professional, outlines new terms and limit, effective date (typically 30 days from notice to allow customer to plan), provides Credit Manager contact for discussion; (c) all notifications tracked in CRM with delivery confirmation
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 10 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1394_Task13" name="Sales team briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Sales team briefing: Credit Manager briefs Head of Trade / Account Management and Regional Sales Managers on significant tier changes (especially downgrades affecting top accounts): (a) coordinate customer communication timing (Sales Rep may want to deliver downgrade news personally to key accounts); (b) discuss credit hold strategy for accounts transitioning to stricter terms
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 1 hour/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1394_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1394_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1394_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1394_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: loses credibility
Owner: Credit Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1394_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1394_Annotation15" targetRef="W1394_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
