    <bpmn:process id="W_W1395" name="W1395. Customer Trade Account Suspension, Reactivation &amp; Delinquent Account Rehabilitation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Credit hold trigger per W572 (automated: payment &gt; 60 days overdue, utilization &gt; 90%, bounced check); or Credit Manager manual suspension decision; or customer requests voluntary suspension
Frequency: ~100–200 account suspensions/year; ~60–120 reactivations/year
Volume: At any given time, ~50–100 accounts are in suspended status
Owner: Credit Manager
Participants: Credit Manager, Credit Analyst, AR Clerk, Sales Rep, Finance Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W1395 — Customer Trade Account Suspension, Reactivation &amp; Delinquent Account Rehabilitation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1395_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1395_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1395_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1395_Lane3" name="Credit Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1395_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1395_Start5" name="Credit hold trigger per W572 (automated: payment &gt; 60 days overdue, utilization &gt; 90%…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1395_Task6" name="Suspension trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Suspension trigger: account enters suspension based on one or more criteria: (a) automated: payment &gt; 60 days overdue and &gt; PHP 50,000 outstanding; (b) automated: credit utilization &gt; 90% for &gt; 30 consecutive days; (c) automated: second bounced check within 6 months (W1381); (d) automated: credit insurer withdraws coverage (W1011); (e) manual: Credit Manager suspends based on adverse information (customer bankruptcy filing, SEC dissolution notice, negative trade references); (f) voluntary: customer requests temporary suspension (e.g., business closed for renovation); system changes account status to &quot;Suspended — Credit Hold&quot;
Responsible (R): System / Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: Automated or 15 min/manual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1395_Task7" name="System enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System enforcement: suspended account cannot process new credit sales — (a) POS: when Cashier enters suspended account at checkout, system displays &quot;Account on Credit Hold — Contact Credit Department&quot; and blocks credit tender; (b) B2B portal: customer cannot place new orders; (c) existing open orders already in fulfillment are reviewed by Credit Manager — allow shipment if &gt; 80% picked, otherwise hold
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task8" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer notification: Credit Analyst contacts customer within 24 hours of suspension: (a) phone call (primary) explaining reason for suspension and required remediation; (b) follow-up email/letter with formal notice, outstanding balance, and remediation requirements; (c) Sales Rep informed simultaneously — Sales Rep may have relationship context that affects the approach
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Sales Rep
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 20 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task9" name="Rehabilitation options">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rehabilitation options: Credit Manager offers remediation path based on reason for suspension: (a) Payment remediation (most common): customer must bring account current (pay all overdue invoices) + provide post-dated checks (W1380) or advance payment for next 3 months as demonstration of commitment; (b) Reduced terms: customer may continue on stricter terms — COD for 3 months, then re-evaluate; (c) Reduced limit: credit limit reduced to 50% of pre-suspension limit, with step-up over 6 months if payments maintained; (d) Collateral/guarantee: for large accounts, customer provides personal guarantee, holdout agreement, or post-dated checks covering 3 months of anticipated purchases
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task10" name="Reactivation criteria">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reactivation criteria: account may be reactivated when: (a) all overdue invoices paid in full; (b) rehabilitation commitment fulfilled (3 months COD maintained, or PDCs provided, or reduced terms payments all on-time); (c) no new bounced checks during rehabilitation period; (d) Credit Analyst reviews updated payment performance and recommends reactivation; (e) Credit Manager approves reactivation with new terms (may be stricter than pre-suspension terms)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 15 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task11" name="System reactivation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: System reactivation: Credit Manager reactivates account in system — (a) status changed to &quot;Active — Rehabilitated&quot;; (b) new credit limit and terms applied; (c) POS block removed; (d) B2B portal access restored; (e) customer notified of reactivation and new terms; (f) account flagged for enhanced monitoring (monthly review instead of quarterly) for 6 months
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task12" name="Permanent suspension / write-off">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Permanent suspension / write-off: if customer fails rehabilitation (does not pay overdue balance within 90 days of suspension, or rehabilitation payments also default): (a) account status changed to &quot;Suspended — Permanent&quot;; (b) Credit Manager initiates collection escalation per W812 (field collection, demand letter, legal referral); (c) if collection fails: bad debt write-off per W81; (d) account permanently blocked from new credit applications
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1395_Task13" name="Monthly suspension dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly suspension dashboard: Credit Manager maintains dashboard showing: (a) accounts currently suspended (count and total outstanding), (b) average days in suspension, (c) reactivation rate (% of suspended accounts successfully rehabilitated within 90 days), (d) permanent suspension and write-off rate, (e) revenue at risk (estimated lost sales from suspended accounts)
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1395_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1395_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1395_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1395_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: Credit Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Credit Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1395_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1395_Annotation15" targetRef="W1395_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
