    <bpmn:process id="W_W1471" name="W1471. Trade Account Consolidated Monthly Billing, Multi-Store Purchase Aggregation &amp; Payment Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: End-of-month billing cycle; or trade customer requests consolidated statement for multiple store purchases
Frequency: Monthly billing cycle; ~5,200 trade accounts; ~3,500 monthly AR invoices per model company profile
Volume: ~3,500 consolidated monthly statements generated; ~2,000 trade accounts purchasing from multiple stores/month
Owner: AR Manager
Participants: AR Analyst, Trade Customer, Store Manager, Credit Analyst, Treasury Analyst, Collections Specialist
Source: workflow W1471 — Trade Account Consolidated Monthly Billing, Multi-Store Purchase Aggregation &amp; Payment Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1471_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1471_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1471_Lane2" name="AR Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1471_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1471_Start4" name="End-of-month billing cycle; or trade customer requests consolidated statement for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1471_Task5" name="Monthly billing cycle initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly billing cycle initiation (1st business day of month): (a) system aggregates all trade account transactions from prior month across all stores: (i) POS charge sales, (ii) project/B2B orders per W112, (iii) delivery charges, (iv) returns and credits per W12, (v) late fees per credit terms; (b) system groups transactions by trade account; (c) for accounts purchasing from multiple stores: system presents consolidated view with store-level breakdown
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1471_Task6" name="Statement generation &amp; validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Statement generation &amp; validation: (a) AR Analyst reviews consolidated statements before distribution: (i) verify opening balance matches prior month&#x27;s closing balance, (ii) verify all transactions are correctly categorized (charges, credits, payments), (iii) check for duplicated transactions (same purchase appearing in two stores — data quality per W1391), (iv) verify credit limit calculation: total outstanding + current month charges ≤ credit limit per W1269; (b) AR Manager approves statement batch for distribution
Responsible (R): AR Analyst
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1471_Task7" name="Statement distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Statement distribution: (a) system auto-generates and sends consolidated statements via: (i) email (PDF attachment with itemized transactions by store), (ii) BuildRight trade portal (online access to current and historical statements per W1117), (iii) optional printed copy mailed to accounts without email; (b) statement includes: summary (opening balance, total charges, total credits/payments, closing balance), store-by-store detail, payment instructions (bank transfer, check, GCash), payment due date per credit terms
Responsible (R): System / AR Analyst
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: Automated + 1 hour spot-check</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1471_Task8" name="Payment receipt &amp; allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment receipt &amp; allocation: (a) trade customer makes payment (bank transfer, check, GCash) referencing account number; (b) Treasury Analyst receives payment notification from bank; (c) AR Analyst allocates payment: (i) for full payment: apply to account — closing balance to zero; (ii) for partial payment: apply per customer instructions (specific invoice/store) or per FIFO (oldest invoices first); (iii) system updates account balance and credit availability in real-time; (d) for multi-store accounts with partial payment: system tracks unallocated balance by store for dispute resolution
Responsible (R): AR Analyst / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: 10 min/payment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1471_Task9" name="Payment discrepancy resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment discrepancy resolution: (a) if customer disputes statement: (i) AR Analyst pulls transaction-level detail from all stores for disputed period, (ii) coordinates with Store Manager(s) to verify transactions — retrieve signed charge slips, delivery receipts, or order confirmations, (iii) if customer is correct: process credit memo and issue revised statement, (iv) if BuildRight is correct: provide supporting documentation to customer; (b) if payment does not match statement amount: (i) investigate: partial payment, bank fees deducted, or customer offset against a credit memo; (ii) resolve and allocate per step 4
Responsible (R): AR Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: 30 min/dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1471_Task10" name="Aging &amp; collection escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Aging &amp; collection escalation: Per W784 collections process: (a) system tracks aging of consolidated account balance: current, 30, 60, 90, 120+ days; (b) for multi-store accounts: aging applies to total consolidated balance, not individual store balances; (c) collections escalation per W784: (i) 30 days: auto-reminder email/SMS, (ii) 60 days: Collections Specialist phone call, (iii) 90 days: credit hold — all stores blocked from charging to account per W1395, (iv) 120+ days: demand letter and potential legal action per W1395
Responsible (R): System / Collections Specialist
Accountable (A): AR Manager
Duration: Per W784</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1471_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1471_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1471_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1471_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: real-time credit check at POS per W1269
Owner: AR Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
