    <bpmn:process id="W_W1472" name="W1472. Trade Account Referral Program, Contractor Network Development &amp; Lead Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade customer refers a new contractor/builder; or Category Manager requests contractor network expansion in a region; or store opening in new market requires trade account pipeline
Frequency: ~100–200 referrals/month chain-wide; ongoing contractor network development; concentrated around new store openings
Volume: ~1,200–2,400 referred leads/year; estimated 30–40% conversion rate to active trade accounts
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter), Category Manager, Credit Analyst, Marketing (campaign support), CRM Specialist
Source: workflow W1472 — Trade Account Referral Program, Contractor Network Development &amp; Lead Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1472_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1472_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1472_Lane2" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1472_Lane3" name="CRM Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1472_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1472_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1472_Start6" name="Trade customer refers a new contractor/builder; or Category Manager requests contractor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1472_Task7" name="Referral program design &amp; communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Referral program design &amp; communication: (a) Category Manager defines referral rewards: (i) referrer receives PHP 500 store credit for each referred lead that opens a trade account, (ii) additional PHP 1,000 store credit when referred account reaches PHP 50,000 in cumulative purchases within 6 months, (iii) referred contractor receives PHP 300 welcome credit on first purchase; (b) Marketing communicates program via: trade account email, store signage at trade counter, CRM notification to all active trade accounts, Facebook trade community groups
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Marketing
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Quarterly review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1472_Task8" name="Referral capture &amp; lead creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Referral capture &amp; lead creation: (a) when a trade customer refers a new contractor: (i) Sales Associate captures referral in CRM: referrer name/account, referred contact name, phone, company, trade type (general contractor, electrician, plumber, etc.), project specialty; (ii) system creates lead record linked to referrer account; (iii) system auto-sends SMS to referred contact: &quot;Welcome! [Referrer] recommended BuildRight Depot for your construction material needs. Visit any store to open your trade account and receive PHP 300 welcome credit.&quot;
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5 min/referral</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1472_Task9" name="Lead nurturing &amp; follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Lead nurturing &amp; follow-up: (a) CRM Specialist tracks referred leads: (i) lead visited store? → proceed to W1269 credit application, (ii) lead not responded within 7 days → Sales Associate follow-up call, (iii) lead not responded within 14 days → second follow-up via SMS with promotional offer, (iv) lead not responded within 30 days → mark as inactive, notify referrer; (b) Category Manager reviews weekly: referral pipeline status, conversion rate, regional gaps in contractor coverage
Responsible (R): CRM Specialist / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1472_Task10" name="Trade account conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Trade account conversion: (a) when referred lead visits store: Sales Associate processes trade account application per W1269 — referral source recorded in application; (b) system auto-credits referrer account with PHP 500 store credit upon new account approval; (c) system auto-credits new account with PHP 300 welcome credit upon first purchase; (d) new account assigned to Store Manager&#x27;s trade portfolio for ongoing relationship management
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Credit Analyst
Duration: Per W1269</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1472_Task11" name="Milestone reward processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Milestone reward processing: (a) system monitors referred account cumulative purchases; (b) when referred account reaches PHP 50,000 within 6 months: system auto-credits referrer account with additional PHP 1,000 store credit; (c) Category Manager notified of milestone for relationship acknowledgment (thank-you call to referrer); (d) if referred account does not reach PHP 50,000 within 6 months: system notifies Sales Associate for follow-up engagement
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1472_Task12" name="Contractor network development analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Contractor network development analytics: (a) monthly: Category Manager reviews referral program performance: (i) referral volume by store and region, (ii) conversion rate (lead → account → active), (iii) referred account retention rate vs. non-referred accounts, (iv) average revenue of referred accounts vs. non-referred, (v) top referrers by volume and quality; (b) quarterly: identify geographic gaps — regions/stores with low trade account penetration targeted for contractor networking events per W148; (c) annually: evaluate program ROI (referral rewards cost vs. new account revenue) and adjust reward structure
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1472_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1472_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1472_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1472_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: TIN/business registration verification during W1269 credit application; operational: first-touch attribution rule (referral record must exist before account application)
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1472_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1472_Annotation14" targetRef="W1472_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow16" sourceRef="W1472_Start6" targetRef="W1472_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow17" sourceRef="W1472_Task7" targetRef="W1472_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow18" sourceRef="W1472_Task8" targetRef="W1472_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow19" sourceRef="W1472_Task9" targetRef="W1472_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow20" sourceRef="W1472_Task10" targetRef="W1472_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow21" sourceRef="W1472_Task11" targetRef="W1472_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1472_Flow22" sourceRef="W1472_Task12" targetRef="W1472_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1472_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1472_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1472">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1472_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1472_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
