    <bpmn:process id="W_W1507" name="W1507. Customer Trade Account Mobile QR-Onboarding &amp; Instant Activation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Contractor, builder, interior designer, or trade professional visits store and expresses interest in trade pricing; or existing walk-in customer&#x27;s purchase pattern triggers trade account eligibility detection at POS
Frequency: ~5–10 new trade account activations per store per year (≈1,000–2,000/year chain-wide per the Volume field)
Volume: ~1,000–2,000 new trade accounts/year chain-wide; target: grow from 5,000 to 7,500 active trade accounts within 2 years
Owner: Sales Associate (in-store); Category Manager (HQ credit approval)
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Category Manager, Credit Analyst (HQ), Customer
Source: workflow W1507 — Customer Trade Account Mobile QR-Onboarding &amp; Instant Activation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1507_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1507_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1507_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1507_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1507_Lane4" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1507_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1507_Start6" name="Contractor, builder, interior designer, or trade professional visits store and expresses…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1507_Task7" name="Trade eligibility detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade eligibility detection: Two triggers: (a) Sales Associate identifies repeat professional customer (contractor badge, bulk purchase, project-specific buying pattern); (b) POS system auto-detects customer purchasing pattern consistent with trade buyers (≥3 visits/month, average transaction ≥PHP 5,000, purchasing in trade categories like lumber, cement, plumbing, electrical) — system prompts cashier: &quot;Customer may qualify for Trade Pricing — ask if they are a trade professional?&quot;
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1507_Task8" name="QR-based application">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: QR-based application: Sales Associate presents QR code on customer-facing display; customer scans with phone camera; mobile web form opens with pre-populated fields: (a) store location, (b) date/time, (c) form captures: full name, trade type (contractor/electrician/plumber/tile setter/interior designer/architect/other), business name (optional), TIN (required), mobile number, email (optional); (d) customer uploads: government ID photo (driver&#x27;s license, passport, or PRC license — required), selfie with ID for verification; (e) customer agrees to trade account terms and conditions (cash-and-carry pricing, no credit, 5–15% discount on eligible items); (f) total form completion: 3–5 minutes on mobile phone
Responsible (R): Customer / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1507_Task9" name="Automated verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Automated verification: System performs real-time verification: (a) TIN format validation per BIR requirements, (b) government ID OCR extraction — verify name matches TIN registration, (c) duplicate check against existing trade account database (same TIN or mobile number), (d) check against negative list (accounts suspended per W1395 for payment defaults or policy violations); (e) verification result: Green (auto-approve) or Yellow (manual review required — ID unclear, TIN mismatch, borderline case)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (30–60 sec)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1507_Task10" name="Instant activation (Green path)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Instant activation (Green path): For auto-approved applications: (a) system creates Trade Account with &quot;Cash-and-Carry&quot; type, (b) generates Trade Account number and QR code card (digital, sent via SMS/email; optional physical card printed at store), (c) account immediately active with standard trade discount tier (5% base discount on eligible items), (d) customer receives SMS confirmation: &quot;Welcome to BuildRight Trade Program! Your account [number] is active. Show your QR code at checkout for trade pricing.&quot;; (e) Sales Associate demonstrates QR code scan at POS — customer&#x27;s first trade-priced transaction can happen immediately
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1507_Task11" name="Manual review (Yellow path)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Manual review (Yellow path): For applications requiring manual review: (a) application routed to Category Manager notification queue, (b) Category Manager reviews within 4 business hours: verify ID quality, assess trade legitimacy, approve or reject with reason, (c) if approved: auto-activation per Step 4; (d) if rejected: customer receives SMS with reason and invitation to re-apply with corrected documents; (e) manual review rate expected at ~15–20% of applications (unclear IDs, unusual trade types, TIN discrepancies)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 5–10 min per review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1507_Task12" name="Post-activation upsell to credit account">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-activation upsell to credit account: Within 30 days of activation, if trade customer&#x27;s monthly purchases exceed PHP 50,000: (a) system flags account for credit upgrade eligibility, (b) Sales Associate or Category Manager contacts customer to offer credit terms per W1269 (Net 30, credit limit based on purchase history), (c) if customer accepts: initiate full credit assessment per W1269; existing trade account converted to credit-bearing account with higher discount tier (10–15%), (d) conversion rate target: 20% of instant-activation accounts upgrade to credit within 12 months
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min per outreach</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1507_Task13" name="Monthly activation analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly activation analytics: Category Manager reviews instant activation program metrics: (a) activation rate by store and region, (b) Green vs. Yellow path ratio, (c) time from scan to first trade purchase, (d) 30-day and 90-day trade customer retention, (e) credit upgrade conversion rate, (f) average monthly spend of instant-activation vs. traditional trade accounts
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1507_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1507_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1507_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1507_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-272 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Management (PA-11.1).) | - operational: selfie-with-ID comparison and manual review for flagged cases; operational: requiring government ID cross-reference; operational: can only validate TIN format, not authenticity
Owner: Sales Associate (in-store); Category Manager (HQ credit approval)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
